# ktm (Ace 6) recovery-side touch enablement.
#
# 1) ODM hbp5 HAL daemon: the ODM-partition binary is not covered by the
#    recovery policy, so init's seclabel audit refuses to start it while
#    the system is enforcing. Enable the generic permissive switch
#    (init.recovery.aera-selinux.rc in bootable/recovery) so the audit
#    becomes non-fatal and the ODM rc can start the daemon.
# 2) HBP IRQ gate: the HBP framework (oplus_hbp_core) registers the
#    touch-00 IRQ at probe time and then disables it; the panel-resume /
#    daemon handshake that normally re-enables it never runs in recovery.
#    Open the device's kernel IRQ gate once AERA module loading is
#    complete so the kernel direct-report path works regardless.

on early-init
    setprop sys.aera.selinux.permissive true

on property:post.decrypt.modules=true
    write /sys/devices/platform/soc/soc:hbp@0/irq_enable 0,1
